## Network
{{ if .Cfg.Firewall.Enabled }}
An egress firewall is **on**. Outbound traffic is restricted to an allowlist:
the Anthropic API, GitHub, and the npm / RubyGems / PyPI / crates registries{{ if .Cfg.Firewall.Allow }},
plus{{ range .Cfg.Firewall.Allow }} `{{ . }}`{{ end }}{{ end }}.

The practical consequence: **`WebFetch` against a domain outside that list fails
with `ECONNREFUSED`**, immediately rather than after a timeout. `WebSearch` runs
server-side and is expected to be unaffected.

If you need a blocked domain, say so and name it. The human can run
`ccic firewall allow <domain>` to add it to the running container in a second,
or `ccic firewall off` for a whole research session. Don't silently give up on a
fetch — a blocked domain is a one-command fix, but only if you mention it.
{{- else }}
The egress firewall is **off** for this project, so outbound traffic is
unrestricted.
{{- end }}

